# Phosphor Icons (Remiix / Faunder UI)

## Always

- Prefer **[Phosphor Icons](https://phosphoricons.com/)** for every new UI icon.
- Find icons with the **`phosphor-icons` MCP** (`search_icons`, `get_icon`). Do not invent path data or pull random icon sets.
- Default weight: **regular**. Use **bold** for small/tab icons when needed. Prefer `fill="#000000"` in the asset so Faunder can recolor via mask/`currentColor`.

## Register for Faunder UI

After picking an icon, **always** add it to [`static/styles/icons.css`](static/styles/icons.css) so markup can use `ui-icon="…"`:

1. Use Phosphor **kebab-case** name as the token (e.g. `magnifying-glass`, `game-controller`).
2. Append a rule matching existing entries:

```css
[ui-icon~="icon-name"] {
  --ui-icon: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%2232%22%20height%3D%2232%22%20fill%3D%22%23000000%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20256%20256%22%3E%3Cpath%20d%3D%22…%22%3E%3C%2Fpath%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E");
}
```

3. URL-encode the SVG for the data URI (`#` → `%23`, `<` → `%3C`, `"` → `%22`, spaces in path as needed).
4. In components, use Faunder: `ui-icon="icon-name"` (optionally with size tokens). Prefer this over inline SVG unless the surface cannot use `ui-icon` (e.g. a one-off that must stay self-contained — still source the path from Phosphor MCP).

## Do not

- Add Lucide / Heroicons / Material / emoji as app chrome icons.
- Duplicate an icon already defined in `icons.css` — reuse the existing token.
- Edit `faunder-ui@….css` for icons; only `static/styles/icons.css`.
